### Description of changes made to the control and datapath to handle hazards and forwarding 
The main changes were done in `hw/hdl/verilog/mips/decode.v`, `mips_cpu.v`, `instruction_fetch.v`, and `alu.v`.

#### Forwarding
- Implemented ID-stage forwarding for both source operands (`rs` and `rt`) from:
  - EX stage result
  - MEM stage writeback value
- Added explicit forwarding priority so EX forwarding takes precedence over MEM forwarding when both match.

#### Stall Logic
- Added load-use hazard detection using `mem_read_ex` and register dependency checks for both `rs` and `rt`.
- Added a store-conditional wait condition so decode stalls when required by LL/SC state.
- Stall behavior uses provided pipeline control (`en_if`, `rst_id`) so stale values are not consumed.

#### Branch/Jump Behavior
- Resolved branch and jump control in ID stage and wired fetch next-PC selection accordingly.
- Added PC selection priority chain for:
  - jump register (`jr`/`jalr`)
  - jump target (`j`/`jal`)
  - branch target
  - sequential PC+4

#### Memory and Subword Operations
- Added/updated support for byte/halfword/word memory behavior:
  - `lb`, `lbu`, `lh`, `sb`, `sh`, `sw`
- Implemented byte and halfword data selection/extension and per-byte write-enable behavior.

#### LL/SC Semantics
- Implemented LL/SC tracking state through decode/execute/memory pipeline.
- `sc` stores only when linked state is valid.
- `sc` writes success/failure result (1/0) to `rt` as required.

### Testing
- Added and updated baseline instruction/unit tests in `sim/tests`.
- Added additional targeted tests to better validate new hazard and memory behavior:
  - `fwd_priority`: verifies EX-vs-MEM forwarding priority
  - `stall_load_xori`: verifies load-use stall with immediate ALU consumer
  - `sh_mask`: verifies halfword store mask behavior (upper/lower half)
  - `lh_offsets_signext`: verifies `lh` offset selection and sign extension

### AI Tool Usage
I used an LLM to help explain how each of the files in the starter code interacted with one another because I was really confused on how they are connected. 

